>> title: Mayu
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: japanese, garlic, ramen, aroma oil, black
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: mayu, 麻油, black garlic oil, burnt garlic oil, ma-yu, black oil, the black float on tonkotsu
>> pairs-with: tonkotsu-ramen
>> servings: 12
>> time: 30 min
>> step.1: A controlled burn: this is supposed to smell scorched, and there are about thirty seconds between right and ruined.
>> step.2: fry to black, 12 min
>> step.3: blitz to a loose black paste
>> step.4: cool and settle 15 min

A controlled burn: this is supposed to smell scorched, and there are about thirty seconds between right and ruined.

Fry @garlic{1%head}(about 12 cloves, minced fine) in @neutral oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL) in a small #saucepan{} over medium-low heat ~fry{12%min}, stirring the whole time. It goes straw, then gold, then chestnut, then black. Gold is not far enough — the bitterness that reads as smoke only arrives at black — and one shade past black is acrid and cannot be diluted back. Take the pan off the heat the moment the colour stops changing quickly.

Blitz @&(~1)black garlic{} with @toasted sesame oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a #blender{} until it is a loose paste with no grit left in it.

Cool @&(~1)mayu{} ~cool{15%min} and let the solids settle. A scant teaspoon goes into a bowl of tonkotsu, drawn across the surface at the last second so it stays a black slick instead of stirring in.
